# CPU dequantization of the admitted GGML block types (PML2-U5 C3, extended
# by GGUF-A3 C1 to the union set {F32, BF16, Q5_0, Q8_0, Q4_K, Q5_K, Q6_K}).
#
# Public import: importa ex "gradus:model/dequant" dequant
# Depends on: nothing (leaf module — self-contained like capsule.fab).
#
# --- Contract ------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Re-expression port (Rust -> Faber) of faber-runtime/src/dequant.rs — the
# GI2-1 CPU dequant core for the admitted SmolLM2-360M-Instruct Q4_K_M row.
# The Rust original is the migration ORACLE (decision pml0-admission-
# migration-decision.md §3.1/§3.2): its tests, fixtures, and pinned-row
# facts are the acceptance target for this port, and this module mirrors
# the dequant trio member 1:1. Supporting surfaces (QuantizedTensorLayout,
# TensorView) stay with their GI owners per §1 — this module owns the
# dequant MATH only: admitted GGML block bytes in, f32 logical elements
# out, fail closed.
#
# CONTRACT — semantics match llama.cpp exactly (`ggml/src/ggml-quants.c`,
# commit `a957b7747` at the pinned checkout): GGML half->f32 (exact
# IEEE-754 binary16->binary32), integer qs, per-block scale/min/dmin/kscale
# application (`dequantize_row_q5_0`, `dequantize_row_q8_0`,
# `dequantize_row_q4_K`, `dequantize_row_q5_K`, `dequantize_row_q6_K` +
# `get_scale_min_k4`, and the bf16 row conversion for GGML_BF16).
# Dequant is exact integer/half math: all arithmetic is plain IEEE-754 f32
# in the same operation order as the C kernels, so outputs are bit-exact
# against the independent reference
# (`radix/docs/factory/gpu-inference-gguf/evidence/gi2-dequant-reference.py`
# and its committed goldens `gi2-dequant-goldens.json`, cited read-only).
#
# FAIL CLOSED:
#   * unknown / un-admitted GGML type id -> TypoIgnotum before any byte is
#     touched (the admitted set is {F32, BF16, Q5_0, Q8_0, Q4_K, Q5_K,
#     Q6_K} — the Qwen3.6 completion-row union set; toy packed-u4 and any
#     other id are un-admitted);
#   * a block whose byte length is not the layout's block_bytes ->
#     GlomulusMala (oracle RowBytesMismatch analog);
#   * a row whose byte length is not a whole multiple of block_bytes ->
#     OrdoMala (oracle BlockBytesMismatch analog);
#   * NaN halves fail closed (ValorMala): the pinned row has none, and a
#     NaN half is malformed data — no bit pattern is smuggled into the
#     dequant output; NaN bf16 values fail closed the same way.
#
# Tensor-level coverage gating (GI1-4 residual: `coverage_ok()` +
# `per_tensor_covered`) is enforced by the admission rows (gguf.fab /
# safetensors.fab) at capsule construction, not re-derived here — this
# module consumes already-validated byte payloads.
#
# --- Compiler boundary notes ----------------------------------------------
#
#   * The language surface has no `f32::from_bits` — binary16->binary32 and
#     binary32-from-4-bytes are computed as exact IEEE values via integer
#     field extraction + power-of-two scaling (same seam as the safetensors
#     f32 decode), which is exact for the finite f32 set.
#   * Proba proof is compile-level until the FMIR stepper / faber test path
#     covers library probas (recorded capsule.fab residual); adfirma
#     assertions run under the auditor-owned `faber test` harness.
#   * Public signatures stay on primitives plus this module's own DequantError
#     so the proba file-interface keeps every export (WARN014 — same seam as
#     capsule.fab U1).
#
# --- Seams ---------------------------------------------------------------
#   * oracle + goldens: faber-runtime/src/dequant.rs, gi2-dequant-goldens.json
#     (read-only; bit-exact comparison is the auditor-owned test path).
#   * tensor-level coverage gate: gguf.fab / safetensors.fab admission.
#   * tokenizer probe parity (P1–P11, workload id lists) — gradus:tokenizer.
#   * negative-matrix conformance suite across U2/U3/U4 — PML2-U6.

# -------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Pinned constants. GGML type ids and block layouts mirror gguf.fab /
# capsule.fab and the pinned toolchain (ggml.h @ a957b7747).
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------

fixum numerus GGML_F32 ← 0
fixum numerus GGML_Q5_0 ← 6
fixum numerus GGML_Q8_0 ← 8
fixum numerus GGML_Q4_K ← 12
fixum numerus GGML_Q5_K ← 13
fixum numerus GGML_Q6_K ← 14
fixum numerus GGML_BF16 ← 30

fixum numerus F32_ELEMENTA ← 1
fixum numerus F32_OCTETI ← 4
fixum numerus BF16_ELEMENTA ← 1
fixum numerus BF16_OCTETI ← 2
fixum numerus Q5_0_ELEMENTA ← 32
fixum numerus Q5_0_OCTETI ← 22
fixum numerus Q8_0_ELEMENTA ← 32
fixum numerus Q8_0_OCTETI ← 34
fixum numerus Q4_K_ELEMENTA ← 256
fixum numerus Q4_K_OCTETI ← 144
fixum numerus Q5_K_ELEMENTA ← 256
fixum numerus Q5_K_OCTETI ← 176
fixum numerus Q6_K_ELEMENTA ← 256
fixum numerus Q6_K_OCTETI ← 210

# -------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DequantError — typed fail-closed diagnostics of the dequant boundary.
# Variant -> class:
#   TypoIgnotum   — un-admitted / unknown GGML type id.
#   GlomulusMala  — block byte length != the layout's block_bytes.
#   OrdoMala      — row byte length not a multiple of block_bytes.
#   ValorMala     — malformed value (NaN half) fails closed.
# The public surface carries @ publica (the post-visibility-flip compiler
# treats unmarked top-level names as module-private); the admitted set and
# every codec below stay importable by the proba and package consumers.
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------

@ publica
discretio DequantError {
    TypoIgnotum { textus causa },
    GlomulusMala { textus causa },
    OrdoMala { textus causa },
    ValorMala { textus causa }
}

@ publica
functio causa(DequantError e) → textus {
    discerne e {
        casu TypoIgnotum fixum causa { redde causa }
        casu GlomulusMala fixum causa { redde causa }
        casu OrdoMala fixum causa { redde causa }
        casu ValorMala fixum causa { redde causa }
    }
}

# -------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Private byte readers (bounds-checked on read; the admission rows have
# already validated the enclosing payload).
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------

@ privata
functio _byte(lista<numerus<u8>> b, numerus off) → numerus {
    redde (b.accipe(off) vel (0 ∷ numerus<u8>)) ↦ numerus
}

@ privata
functio _le_u16(lista<numerus<u8>> b, numerus off) → numerus {
    redde _byte(b, off) ∨ (_byte(b, off + 1) ⇐ 8)
}

@ privata
functio _le_u32(lista<numerus<u8>> b, numerus off) → numerus {
    redde _byte(b, off) ∨ (_byte(b, off + 1) ⇐ 8) ∨ (_byte(b, off + 2) ⇐ 16) ∨ (_byte(b, off + 3) ⇐ 24)
}

# Unsigned byte -> signed i8 value.
@ privata
functio _i8(numerus v) → numerus {
    si v ≥ 128 ergo redde v - 256
    redde v
}

# Compute 2^n via repeated multiplication/division. n range: [-127, 128]
# — matches the IEEE-754 exponent spans this module needs.
@ privata
functio _potentia_duorum(numerus n) → fractus {
    varia fractus result ← 1.0
    si n ≥ 0 {
        varia numerus i ← 0
        dum i < n {
            result ← result * 2.0
            i ← i + 1
        }
    } secus {
        varia numerus i ← n
        dum i < 0 {
            result ← result / 2.0
            i ← i + 1
        }
    }
    redde result
}

# -------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GGML half (binary16) -> exact f32 VALUE (no bit reinterpretation — value
# arithmetic, exact for every finite half). Fail closed on NaN halves.
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------

@ privata
functio _dimidium(lista<numerus<u8>> b, numerus off) → f32 ⇥ DequantError {
    fixum numerus bits ← _le_u16(b, off)
    fixum numerus sign ← (bits ⇒ 15) % 2
    fixum numerus exp ← (bits ⇒ 10) % 32
    fixum numerus frac ← bits % 1024

    varia fractus sign_factor ← 1.0
    si sign ≠ 0 {
        sign_factor ← -1.0
    }

    si exp ≡ 0 {
        si frac ≡ 0 {
            # ±0 (subnormal zero)
            redde (sign_factor * 0.0) ↦ f32
        }
        # Subnormal: ±frac × 2^-24
        fixum fractus power ← _potentia_duorum(-24)
        redde (sign_factor * power * (frac ↦ fractus)) ↦ f32
    }

    si exp ≡ 31 {
        si frac ≡ 0 {
            # ±inf via f64 overflow -> f32 narrowing (same seam as the
            # safetensors f32 decode).
            fixum fractus power ← _potentia_duorum(128)
            redde (sign_factor * power * 2.0) ↦ f32
        }
        iace finge ValorMala { causa = "NaN half in dequant block" }
    }

    # Normal: ±2^(e-15) × (1 + frac/1024)
    fixum fractus power ← _potentia_duorum(exp - 15)
    fixum fractus frac_ratio ← (frac ↦ fractus) / 1024.0
    redde (sign_factor * power * (1.0 + frac_ratio)) ↦ f32
}

# GGML bf16 -> exact f32 VALUE. bf16 is sign(1) / exponent(8, bias 127) /
# mantissa(7): value-arithmetic decode through the same `_potentia_duorum`
# seam as `_dimidium` (bit-exact for every finite bf16, which is exactly
# representable in f32). ±inf via f64 overflow narrowing; NaN fails closed.
@ privata
functio _bfloat16(lista<numerus<u8>> b, numerus off) → f32 ⇥ DequantError {
    fixum numerus bits ← _le_u16(b, off)
    fixum numerus sign ← (bits ⇒ 15) % 2
    fixum numerus exp ← (bits ⇒ 7) % 256
    fixum numerus frac ← bits % 128

    varia fractus sign_factor ← 1.0
    si sign ≠ 0 {
        sign_factor ← -1.0
    }

    si exp ≡ 0 {
        si frac ≡ 0 {
            # ±0 (subnormal zero)
            redde (sign_factor * 0.0) ↦ f32
        }
        # Subnormal: ±frac × 2^-126 × 2^-7
        fixum fractus power ← _potentia_duorum(-126)
        redde (sign_factor * power * ((frac ↦ fractus) / 128.0)) ↦ f32
    }

    si exp ≡ 255 {
        si frac ≡ 0 {
            # ±inf via f64 overflow -> f32 narrowing.
            fixum fractus power ← _potentia_duorum(128)
            redde (sign_factor * power * 2.0) ↦ f32
        }
        iace finge ValorMala { causa = "NaN bf16 value in dequant block" }
    }

    # Normal: ±2^(e-127) × (1 + frac/128)
    fixum fractus power ← _potentia_duorum(exp - 127)
    fixum fractus frac_ratio ← (frac ↦ fractus) / 128.0
    redde (sign_factor * power * (1.0 + frac_ratio)) ↦ f32
}

# 4 little-endian bytes -> exact f32 VALUE (IEEE-754 binary32 decode, the
# same seam as the safetensors `_f32le_quattuor`; NaN fails closed).
@ privata
functio _f32le(lista<numerus<u8>> b, numerus off) → f32 ⇥ DequantError {
    fixum numerus b0 ← _byte(b, off)
    fixum numerus b1 ← _byte(b, off + 1)
    fixum numerus b2 ← _byte(b, off + 2)
    fixum numerus b3 ← _byte(b, off + 3)

    fixum numerus raw ← (b3 * 16777216) + (b2 * 65536) + (b1 * 256) + b0

    fixum numerus sign ← (raw ⇒ 31) % 2
    fixum numerus exp ← (raw ⇒ 23) % 256
    fixum numerus frac ← raw % 8388608

    varia fractus sign_factor ← 1.0
    si sign ≠ 0 {
        sign_factor ← -1.0
    }
    fixum fractus frac_ratio ← (frac ↦ fractus) / 8388608.0

    si exp ≡ 0 {
        si frac ≡ 0 {
            redde (sign_factor * 0.0) ↦ f32
        }
        fixum fractus power ← _potentia_duorum(-126)
        redde (sign_factor * power * frac_ratio) ↦ f32
    }

    si exp ≡ 255 {
        si frac ≡ 0 {
            fixum fractus power ← _potentia_duorum(128)
            redde (sign_factor * power * 2.0) ↦ f32
        }
        iace finge ValorMala { causa = "NaN f32 value in dequant block" }
    }

    fixum fractus power ← _potentia_duorum(exp - 127)
    redde (sign_factor * power * (1.0 + frac_ratio)) ↦ f32
}

# -------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Block kernels — mirror dequant.rs / llama.cpp exactly (same operation
# order; all arithmetic in f32).
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------

# `block_q8_0`: d (half) + qs[32] int8 -> y[j] = qs[j] * d.
@ privata
functio _dequant_q8_0(lista<numerus<u8>> b) → lista<f32> ⇥ DequantError {
    fixum f32 d ← _dimidium(b, 0)
    varia lista<f32> y ← vacua
    varia numerus j ← 0
    dum j < 32 {
        y.appende((_i8(_byte(b, 2 + j)) ↦ f32) * d)
        j ← j + 1
    }
    redde y
}

# `block_q5_0`: d (half) + qh[4] bitmask + qs[16] nibbles. Output order
# matches llama.cpp: y[0..16] from the low nibbles, y[16..32] from the
# high nibbles (two 16-elem runs, appended in that order).
@ privata
functio _dequant_q5_0(lista<numerus<u8>> b) → lista<f32> ⇥ DequantError {
    fixum f32 d ← _dimidium(b, 0)
    fixum numerus qh ← _le_u32(b, 2)
    varia lista<f32> low ← vacua
    varia lista<f32> high ← vacua
    varia numerus j ← 0
    dum j < 16 {
        # xh_0 = ((qh >> j) << 4) & 0x10 ; xh_1 = (qh >> (j+12)) & 0x10
        fixum numerus xh_0 ← ((qh ⇒ j) % 2) * 16
        fixum numerus xh_1 ← ((qh ⇒ (j + 16)) % 2) * 16
        fixum numerus qs ← _byte(b, 6 + j)
        fixum numerus x0 ← ((qs % 16) ∨ xh_0) - 16
        fixum numerus x1 ← (((qs ⇒ 4) % 16) ∨ xh_1) - 16
        low.appende((x0 ↦ f32) * d)
        high.appende((x1 ↦ f32) * d)
        j ← j + 1
    }
    varia lista<f32> y ← vacua
    itera ex low fixum v {
        y.appende(v)
    }
    itera ex high fixum v {
        y.appende(v)
    }
    redde y
}

# `get_scale_min_k4` (llama.cpp ggml-quants.c): 6-bit scale + 6-bit min
# from scales[K_SCALE_SIZE = 12]. The scales array lives at block offset 4
# (the caller's `b`); indexes are relative to that array. Returns (sc, m).
# For index >= 4 the high-bit halves are 2 bits each: `(scales[j-4] >> 6)
# << 4` / `(scales[j] >> 6) << 4` — kept as `% 4` so both bits survive.
@ privata
genus ScalaMinima {
    numerus sc
    numerus m
}

@ privata
functio _scala_minima_k4(numerus index, lista<numerus<u8>> b) → ScalaMinima {
    si index < 4 {
        redde ScalaMinima {
            sc = _byte(b, 4 + index) % 64,
            m = _byte(b, 8 + index) % 64
        }
    }
    fixum numerus sc ← ((_byte(b, 8 + index) % 16) ∨ (((_byte(b, index) ⇒ 6) % 4) * 16))
    fixum numerus m ← (((_byte(b, 8 + index) ⇒ 4) % 16) ∨ (((_byte(b, 4 + index) ⇒ 6) % 4) * 16))
    redde ScalaMinima { sc = sc, m = m }
}

# `block_q4_K`: d, dmin (halves), scales[12], qs[128]. Per 64-element
# sub-block pair: d1 = d·sc(is), m1 = dmin·m(is), d2 = d·sc(is+1),
# m2 = dmin·m(is+1); y = d1·(qs&0xF) − m1 for 32 elements, then
# y = d2·(qs>>4) − m2 for 32. Output per chunk is one 64-elem run:
# first the 32 low-nibble values, then the 32 high-nibble values.
@ privata
functio _dequant_q4_k(lista<numerus<u8>> b) → lista<f32> ⇥ DequantError {
    fixum f32 d ← _dimidium(b, 0)
    fixum f32 dmin ← _dimidium(b, 2)
    varia lista<f32> y ← vacua
    varia numerus is ← 0
    varia numerus qoff ← 0
    varia numerus chunk ← 0
    dum chunk < 4 {
        fixum ScalaMinima sm0 ← _scala_minima_k4(is, b)
        fixum f32 d1 ← d * (sm0.sc ↦ f32)
        fixum f32 m1 ← dmin * (sm0.m ↦ f32)
        fixum ScalaMinima sm1 ← _scala_minima_k4(is + 1, b)
        fixum f32 d2 ← d * (sm1.sc ↦ f32)
        fixum f32 m2 ← dmin * (sm1.m ↦ f32)
        varia lista<f32> low ← vacua
        varia lista<f32> high ← vacua
        varia numerus l ← 0
        dum l < 32 {
            fixum numerus qs ← _byte(b, 16 + qoff + l)
            low.appende(d1 * ((qs % 16) ↦ f32) - m1)
            high.appende(d2 * (((qs ⇒ 4) % 16) ↦ f32) - m2)
            l ← l + 1
        }
        itera ex low fixum v {
            y.appende(v)
        }
        itera ex high fixum v {
            y.appende(v)
        }
        qoff ← qoff + 32
        is ← is + 2
        chunk ← chunk + 1
    }
    redde y
}

# `block_q5_K`: d, dmin (halves), scales[12], qh[32] high bits, qs[128]
# nibbles. Per 64-element sub-block pair: d1 = d·sc(is), m1 = dmin·m(is),
# d2 = d·sc(is+1), m2 = dmin·m(is+1); the qh byte at index l supplies the
# 5th bit of each nibble (bit 2c for the low nibble, bit 2c+1 for the high
# nibble, c = chunk index). y = d1·qs16 − m1 for 32 elements, then
# y = d2·qs16 − m2 for 32 — same output order as llama.cpp's
# `dequantize_row_q5_K` (two 32-elem runs per chunk, low then high).
@ privata
functio _dequant_q5_k(lista<numerus<u8>> b) → lista<f32> ⇥ DequantError {
    fixum f32 d ← _dimidium(b, 0)
    fixum f32 dmin ← _dimidium(b, 2)
    varia lista<f32> y ← vacua
    varia numerus is ← 0
    varia numerus qoff ← 0
    varia numerus chunk ← 0
    dum chunk < 4 {
        fixum ScalaMinima sm0 ← _scala_minima_k4(is, b)
        fixum f32 d1 ← d * (sm0.sc ↦ f32)
        fixum f32 m1 ← dmin * (sm0.m ↦ f32)
        fixum ScalaMinima sm1 ← _scala_minima_k4(is + 1, b)
        fixum f32 d2 ← d * (sm1.sc ↦ f32)
        fixum f32 m2 ← dmin * (sm1.m ↦ f32)
        varia lista<f32> low ← vacua
        varia lista<f32> high ← vacua
        varia numerus l ← 0
        dum l < 32 {
            fixum numerus qs ← _byte(b, 48 + qoff + l)
            fixum numerus qh ← _byte(b, 16 + l)
            # 5th bits: bit 2c (low nibble) / bit 2c+1 (high nibble).
            fixum numerus hi_lo ← ((qh ⇒ (2 * chunk)) % 2) * 16
            fixum numerus hi_hi ← ((qh ⇒ (2 * chunk + 1)) % 2) * 16
            fixum numerus qs16_lo ← (qs % 16) ∨ hi_lo
            fixum numerus qs16_hi ← ((qs ⇒ 4) % 16) ∨ hi_hi
            low.appende(d1 * (qs16_lo ↦ f32) - m1)
            high.appende(d2 * (qs16_hi ↦ f32) - m2)
            l ← l + 1
        }
        itera ex low fixum v {
            y.appende(v)
        }
        itera ex high fixum v {
            y.appende(v)
        }
        qoff ← qoff + 32
        is ← is + 2
        chunk ← chunk + 1
    }
    redde y
}

# `block_q6_K`: ql[128] low nibbles, qh[64] high bits, scales[16] int8,
# d (half) at byte offset 208. Output order matches llama.cpp: within
# each 128-element group the four quants are written at strides 0/32/64/96
# over l — one 32-elem run per stride, appended in stride order.
@ privata
functio _dequant_q6_k(lista<numerus<u8>> b) → lista<f32> ⇥ DequantError {
    fixum f32 d ← _dimidium(b, 208)
    varia lista<f32> y ← vacua
    varia numerus n ← 0
    dum n < 2 {
        fixum numerus sc_base ← n * 8
        fixum numerus ql_off ← n * 64
        fixum numerus qh_off ← n * 32
        varia lista<f32> q1s ← vacua
        varia lista<f32> q2s ← vacua
        varia lista<f32> q3s ← vacua
        varia lista<f32> q4s ← vacua
        varia numerus l ← 0
        dum l < 32 {
            fixum numerus is ← l / 16
            fixum numerus ql_lo ← _byte(b, ql_off + l)
            fixum numerus ql_hi ← _byte(b, ql_off + l + 32)
            fixum numerus qh ← _byte(b, 128 + qh_off + l)
            # q1..q4: low/high nibbles + 2-bit high groups, then -32.
            fixum numerus q1 ← ((ql_lo % 16) ∨ ((qh % 4) * 16)) - 32
            fixum numerus q2 ← ((ql_hi % 16) ∨ (((qh ⇒ 2) % 4) * 16)) - 32
            fixum numerus q3 ← (((ql_lo ⇒ 4) % 16) ∨ (((qh ⇒ 4) % 4) * 16)) - 32
            fixum numerus q4 ← (((ql_hi ⇒ 4) % 16) ∨ (((qh ⇒ 6) % 4) * 16)) - 32
            fixum f32 sc0 ← (_i8(_byte(b, 192 + sc_base + is + 0)) ↦ f32)
            fixum f32 sc2 ← (_i8(_byte(b, 192 + sc_base + is + 2)) ↦ f32)
            fixum f32 sc4 ← (_i8(_byte(b, 192 + sc_base + is + 4)) ↦ f32)
            fixum f32 sc6 ← (_i8(_byte(b, 192 + sc_base + is + 6)) ↦ f32)
            # Same left-associative f32 multiplication order as the C
            # kernels ((d * sc) * q), so outputs are bit-exact.
            q1s.appende(d * sc0 * (q1 ↦ f32))
            q2s.appende(d * sc2 * (q2 ↦ f32))
            q3s.appende(d * sc4 * (q3 ↦ f32))
            q4s.appende(d * sc6 * (q4 ↦ f32))
            l ← l + 1
        }
        itera ex q1s fixum v {
            y.appende(v)
        }
        itera ex q2s fixum v {
            y.appende(v)
        }
        itera ex q3s fixum v {
            y.appende(v)
        }
        itera ex q4s fixum v {
            y.appende(v)
        }
        n ← n + 1
    }
    redde y
}

# F32 scalar block: bit-exact passthrough of the 4 little-endian bytes.
@ privata
functio _dequant_f32(lista<numerus<u8>> b) → lista<f32> ⇥ DequantError {
    varia lista<f32> y ← vacua
    y.appende(_f32le(b, 0))
    redde y
}

# BF16 scalar block: one bf16 value (2 LE bytes) -> exact f32 value.
@ privata
functio _dequant_bf16(lista<numerus<u8>> b) → lista<f32> ⇥ DequantError {
    varia lista<f32> y ← vacua
    y.appende(_bfloat16(b, 0))
    redde y
}

# -------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Layout facts (block elements / block bytes per admitted type; 0 for
# un-admitted types). Public so the row entry point and the admission
# consumers can compute block counts without re-deriving the table.
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------

@ publica
functio elementa_glomoris(numerus typo) → numerus {
    si typo ≡ GGML_F32 ergo redde F32_ELEMENTA
    si typo ≡ GGML_BF16 ergo redde BF16_ELEMENTA
    si typo ≡ GGML_Q5_0 ergo redde Q5_0_ELEMENTA
    si typo ≡ GGML_Q8_0 ergo redde Q8_0_ELEMENTA
    si typo ≡ GGML_Q4_K ergo redde Q4_K_ELEMENTA
    si typo ≡ GGML_Q5_K ergo redde Q5_K_ELEMENTA
    si typo ≡ GGML_Q6_K ergo redde Q6_K_ELEMENTA
    redde 0
}

@ publica
functio octeti_glomoris(numerus typo) → numerus {
    si typo ≡ GGML_F32 ergo redde F32_OCTETI
    si typo ≡ GGML_BF16 ergo redde BF16_OCTETI
    si typo ≡ GGML_Q5_0 ergo redde Q5_0_OCTETI
    si typo ≡ GGML_Q8_0 ergo redde Q8_0_OCTETI
    si typo ≡ GGML_Q4_K ergo redde Q4_K_OCTETI
    si typo ≡ GGML_Q5_K ergo redde Q5_K_OCTETI
    si typo ≡ GGML_Q6_K ergo redde Q6_K_OCTETI
    redde 0
}

# -------------------------------------------------------------------------
# dequantizas_glomulus — dequantize ONE admitted GGML block to its f32
# logical elements. Fail closed on un-admitted type (before any byte is
# touched) and on block byte-length mismatch.
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------

@ publica
functio dequantizas_glomulus(numerus typo, lista<numerus<u8>> blocci) → lista<f32> ⇥ DequantError {
    fixum numerus elementa ← elementa_glomoris(typo)
    si elementa ≡ 0 {
        iace finge TypoIgnotum { causa = "un-admitted GGML type id: " + (typo ↦ textus) }
    }
    fixum numerus blocci_octeti ← octeti_glomoris(typo)
    si blocci.longitudo() ≠ blocci_octeti {
        iace finge GlomulusMala { causa = "block byte length mismatch" }
    }

    si typo ≡ GGML_F32 ergo redde _dequant_f32(blocci)
    si typo ≡ GGML_BF16 ergo redde _dequant_bf16(blocci)
    si typo ≡ GGML_Q5_0 ergo redde _dequant_q5_0(blocci)
    si typo ≡ GGML_Q8_0 ergo redde _dequant_q8_0(blocci)
    si typo ≡ GGML_Q4_K ergo redde _dequant_q4_k(blocci)
    si typo ≡ GGML_Q5_K ergo redde _dequant_q5_k(blocci)
    si typo ≡ GGML_Q6_K ergo redde _dequant_q6_k(blocci)
    iace finge TypoIgnotum { causa = "unreachable" }
}

# -------------------------------------------------------------------------
# dequantizas_ordo — dequantize a packed row (blocks × block_bytes, the
# GGUF data-region payload of one admitted tensor) to its f32 logical
# elements, in GGUF block order. Fail closed on un-admitted type and on a
# row byte length that is not a whole multiple of block_bytes.
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------

@ publica
functio dequantizas_ordo(numerus typo, lista<numerus<u8>> octeti) → lista<f32> ⇥ DequantError {
    fixum numerus elementa ← elementa_glomoris(typo)
    si elementa ≡ 0 {
        iace finge TypoIgnotum { causa = "un-admitted GGML type id: " + (typo ↦ textus) }
    }
    fixum numerus blocci_octeti ← octeti_glomoris(typo)
    si octeti.longitudo() % blocci_octeti ≠ 0 {
        iace finge OrdoMala { causa = "row byte length not a multiple of block_bytes" }
    }

    varia lista<f32> y ← vacua
    varia numerus off ← 0
    dum off < octeti.longitudo() {
        varia lista<numerus<u8>> blocci ← vacua
        varia numerus i ← 0
        dum i < blocci_octeti {
            blocci.appende(octeti.accipe(off + i) vel (0 ∷ numerus<u8>))
            i ← i + 1
        }
        fixum lista<f32> g ← dequantizas_glomulus(typo, blocci)
        itera ex g fixum v {
            y.appende(v)
        }
        off ← off + blocci_octeti
    }
    redde y
}
